\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Bank of Russia Defends Ruble for First Time in 5 Months in April\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2013\par 17:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in five months to ease downward pressure on the ruble, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $663.1 million and 45.1 million euros ($59.1 million) from foreign exchanges reserves in April to smooth ruble volatility. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, after buying $714.9 million and EUR72.6 million in the first two months of 2013.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aiming to switch to a policy of inflation targeting over the next two years, is gradually paring its presence in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Higher flexibility of the ruble exchange rate makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  an absorber of external shocks, related to commodity market volatility, which are crucial for balance of payments in one of the world's largest oil and gas producers.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the ruble within a corridor of RUB31.65-RUB38.65 against a euro-dollar basket, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars and euros when the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades in the lower half of the range to avoid excessive ruble appreciation, while it sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble hovers in the upper half of the band.\par \par \uc2 The bank is inactive if the ruble trades between RUB34.65 and RUB35.65 versus the basket of $0.55 and EUR0.45.\par \par \uc2 In early April, the ruble weakened beyond RUB35.65 following a fall in oil prices amid rising global risk aversion, but returned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -free zone April 25.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 07, 2013 11:25 ET (15:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130507e95700402\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
