\par\par \b \uc2 Falling Ruble Prompts  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2013\par 13:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ease downside pressure on the ruble for the first time since November, the bank's data showed Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 30 million rubles ($0.95 million) on the Moscow exchange Wednesday when the ruble dropped after the finance ministry said it will start buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the open market in the second half of 2013 to boost liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intention to cut lending rates as inflation slows also put pressure on the ruble. Lower lending rates mean the ruble and ruble-denominated assets become less attractive for using in carry trade where low yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are used to buy into higher-yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 "[The] ruble is under pressure which comes from everywhere," analysts at Nordea bank said in a note, pointing to a slump in oil prices, the ruble's key benchmark, and expectations of a rate cut.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the ruble within a corridor against the euro-dollar basket of $0.55 and 0.45 euros. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its reserves when the ruble weakens, moving closer to the upper half of the corridor, and buys dollars and euros when the ruble firms towards the lower half of the band.\par \par \uc2 In the middle of the corridor between RUB34.65 and RUB35.65, where the ruble has traded since the middle of November, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruble is on track to stage its biggest weekly drop against the basket since August. In the five days to April 5 the ruble has already lost 2.1% versus the basket, hovering at around RUB35.72 as of 1020 GMT, its weakest since mid-September.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the ruble gained 0.1% against the dollar to RUB31.55, after touching its lowest level since November at RUB31.75 earlier this week. Against the euro Friday, the ruble was steady at RUB40.82, close to its weakest point since January of RUB40.86 hit this week.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Rosbank said in a note that the ruble could rebound from multi-month lows but given all risks it is better not to open long positions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the near term the ruble can stabilize at around RUB35.7-RUB36.0 versus the basket and in the range of RUB31.7-RUB32.0 against the dollar, said Nordea bank.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com [ 05-04-13 1105GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130405e945000fw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
