\par\par \b \uc2 Russian markets - Factors to Watch on February 14\b0\par\par\uc2 741 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2013\par 07:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Here are events and news stories that could move Russian markets on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 You can reach us on: +7 495 775 1242.\par \par \uc2 STOCKS CALL (Contributions to moscow.newsroom@reuters.com):\par \par \uc2 ALFA BANK\uc2 : "This morning Asia is up after weak Japanese data fuelling stimulus hopes, while US and European equity futures are pointing sideways ... Today, we will see 4Q GDP figures for the Eurozone and its members as well as jobless claims in the US."\par \par \uc2 URALSIB: "Commodities are stable this morning as Asian markets also in a positive mood. However, we expect the Micex to open down 0.3% and take a breather after yesterday's rally."\par \par \uc2 EVENTS (All times GMT):\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  meets OECD secretary general;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Putin meets FSB officials to sum up their work in 2012 and give guidance for 2013;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - The Moscow Exchange is closing order books for its initial public offering;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Institute of International Finance is organising a conference ahead of the G20 meeting of finance ministers and central bankers in Moscow;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Derivatives in Russia 2013 conference;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to publish its weekly gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - \uc2 World Bank\uc2 's President \uc2 Jim Yong Kim\uc2  to deliver a lecture in Moscow;\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK - \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 , the world's top gas producer, to hold investor day.\par \par \uc2 IN THE PAPERS :\par \par \uc2 The owners of \uc2 Norilsk Nickel\uc2  are in talks to acquire \uc2 Metalloinvest\uc2 's Udokan copper deposit in exchange for an increased stake in the Russian nickel and palladium mining giant, the \uc2 Kommersant\uc2  daily said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Vedomosti runs an interview with Albert Shigabutdinov, chief executive with Taif company, with \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in oil refining, oil chemistry and some others.\par \par \uc2 TOP STORIES IN RUSSIA AND THE CIS :\par \par \uc2 TOP NEWS: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par G20 chair Russia backs G7 statement on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      \par G20 host Russia struggles with chronic investor mistrust         \par Putin cautious as Rosneft urges broader LNG rights               \par Bolshoi Ballet chief's sight recovering after acid attack        \par Russia plans $25-$30 bln oil-for-loans deal with China           \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Important that Japan hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on yen            \par COMPANIES/MARKETS: \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Metalloinvest\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise Norilsk stake via Udokan swap-paper      \par Exxon, Rosneft mull plant to liquefy Sakhalin gas                \par Finland retailer Stockmann's Q4 profit misses forecast           \par Russian car recycling levy shreds free-trade                     \par Moscow bourse IPO fully subscribed with state fund backing-cbank \par Russia's LUKOIL eyes Brazilian offshore oil and gas              \par Russian finmin may convert windfall revenues via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 fx\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market       \par Short squeeze lifts Russian stocks to one-week highs             \par Russian retailer Dixy says January sales rise 22.1 pct           \par Rosneft board approves $14.2 bln loan for \f28 \uc2 \f2 TNK-BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  deal            \par  \par ECONOMY/POLITICS: \par Azeri party offers bounty for ear of author           