\par\par \b \uc2 Russian finmin may convert windfall revenues via  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2013\par 17:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2013 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Sovereign funds now held at c.bank\par \par \uc2 * Transfers done off market\par \par \uc2 * Hold combined $174 billion in assets\par \par \uc2 By Katya Golubkova and Maya Dyakina\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 13 (Reuters) - \uc2 Russia's Finance Ministry\uc2  said on Wednesday it was considering a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposal for the ministry to convert windfall oil revenues on its own openly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Such a step would separate the government's management of its sovereign wealth funds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is gradually increasing the freedom with which it allows the rouble to float.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has scaled back its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to the point where it was hardly present on the market in the final quarter of last year, as it turns its focus towards Western-style inflation-targeting.\par \par \uc2 Currently, \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts as the agent to convert rouble oil and gas proceeds into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the Finance Ministry in off-market transactions.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indeed addressed this proposal to us. It has its reasons, it is very interesting, we are considering it at the moment, there is no decision taken," Deputy Finance Minister Alexei Moiseyev told reporters. No reason was given for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposal.\par \par \uc2 The proposed move would potentially soften \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as the regulator struggles to focus on inflation.\par \par \uc2 "The transactions conducted by the finance ministry bypassing the market ... affect the money supply and may have inflationary consequences," said Alexander Morozov , chief economist for Russia and CIS at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Fund and the second outlet for Russia's windfall oil revenue, the National Welfare Fund (NWF), are kept 45 percent in euros, 45 percent in dollars and 10 percent in sterling and total 8.5 percent of GDP.\par \par \uc2 The two sovereign wealth funds hold a combined 5.3 trillion roubles ($176 billion), and are counted towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which totalled $534 billion at the last count.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Fund was created as a safety net against external shocks such as falls in global oil prices, while the NWF is designed to cover deficits in the pension system and is mostly invested in the bonds of Western governments.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry transfers oil and gas proceeds which come above budget target to the Reserve Fund once a year in February via off-market exchanges with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Extra demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , all things being equal, would contribute to weakening of the rouble when oil prices are high," Morozov said.\par \par \uc2 "But when Russia needs money from the Reserve Fund to patch holes in the budget, the finance minister would step in to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is quite reasonable and countercyclical."\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 30.0560 Russian roubles)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Oksana Kobzeva; writing by Maya Dyakina; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/FINMIN | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130216e92d0007m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
