\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble at Six-Week High vs Dollar on Fiscal Cliff Hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2012\par 16:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Russian ruble rallied against the dollar to its strongest level in six weeks Thursday, boosted by last month-end tax payments and expectations that the U.S. will resolve its "fiscal cliff" issues.\par \par \uc2 The ruble gained 1.2% to RUB30.80 against the dollar, its strongest level since Oct. 19, before easing slightly to 30.83 by 1403 GMT. Against the euro, the ruble strengthened 0.36% to RUB40.04.\par \par \uc2 "The ruble's firming is driven by a spike in optimism about the U.S. It's obvious that neither the U.S. nor the global economy would allow a slump, and the ruble, as a risky \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is gaining from that," said Dmitry Novoselov, head of derivative sales at Nordea in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week U.S. House of Representatives Speaker \uc2 John Boehner\uc2  said he is optimistic a deal over the so-called fiscal cliff could be reached, and U.S. President Barack Obama said he is hopeful the White House and Congress can reach a deal by Christmas.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro-dollar basket, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gauge of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the ruble strengthened 0.6% to RUB35.0, remaining in the range of RUB34.65-RUB35.65, in which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Local month-end taxes also worked in the ruble's favor, as they prompted export-focused companies to convert dollars and euros to meet local liability.\par \par \uc2 The ruble could strengthen to RUB34.6 against the basket in the near term before easing gradually to around RUB35.0 by the end of December, analysts at Raiffeisen said.\par \par \uc2 "We are entering the last month of the year and people usually prefer piling up hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the eve of super-long holidays," Mr. Novoselov said, referring to Russia's annual New Year holidays. Russian markets will close Dec. 30 and won't open again until Jan. 9.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com [ 29-11-12 1510GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121129e8bt000tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
