\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Firms Beyond RUB31 Vs Dollar Before Greece Aid Decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2012\par 11:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble firmed beyond the psychologically important level of RUB31 per dollar Monday, boosted by local month-end taxes and expectations that European leaders will approve a next aid package for Greece.\par \par \uc2 The ruble firmed 0.3% versus the dollar to RUB30.94, it's strongest level since Oct. 22, and was steady at RUB40.18 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The ruble's appreciation is quite logical given rising amount of corporate selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and expectations of a global rally," said Pavel Demeshchik, a dealer at ING in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 This week Russian companies will have to pay mineral extraction tax, excise duties and profit tax, for which export-focused firms are converting dollars and euros to meet local liabilities.\par \par \uc2 Market players are closely watching the outcome of talks between euro-zone finance ministers and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  about a 44.6 billion euros ($57.9 billion) loan to Greece.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Demeshchik said the ruble could get further support if the result of European negotiations is positive or at least neutral, while the volatility is likely to rise later in the day after the U.S. market opens.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro-dollar basket, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's barometer of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the ruble gained 0.1% to RUB35.13, remaining in the range of 34.65-35.65, where the Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't carry out any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If external markets will at least retain current mood ruble basket can make an attempt to [strengthen] further to RUB35. Oil prices are very supportive," analysts at Nordea said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com [ 26-11-12 1017GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121126e8bq000it\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
