\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  CB May Continue  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Interventions \highlight\uc2  Beyond 2015- Dep Head\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alexander Kolyandr  \par \uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2012\par 11:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The deputy chairman of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested Tuesday that the bank may continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets even after the ruble becomes fully free-floating, expected in 2015.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not "obliged to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " beyond 2015 and may continue to wade into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth volatility, said Alexey Ulyukayev.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the ruble within a floating range against the euro and the dollar.\par \par \uc2 He also said Russian inflation may slightly exceed the target range for 2012, he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had projected 2012 inflation at 5% to 6% while the economic development ministry has it at 7%.\par \par \uc2 He spoke at an investment forum organized by the Russian bank VTB (VTBR.RS).\par \par \uc2 Write to Alexander Kolyandr at alexander.kolyandr@dowjones.com (Olga Razumovskaya contributed to the story.) [ 02-10-12 0944GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121002e8a2000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
