\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian shares continue rally, rouble firms on oil\b0\par\par\uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2012\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Rouble edge up vs dollar on oil\par \par \uc2  * Stocks indexes creep higher\par \par \uc2  * Worries about euro zone, China growth weigh \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, detail, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Russian shares extended fragile gains on Monday, helped by a buoyant mood on global markets, while the rouble inched higher, catching up with an oil price recovery.\par \par \uc2  At 1423 GMT, the rouble-denominated MICEX exchange rose 1.9 percent to 1,485.9 points. The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 2.4 percent to 1,511.1. \par \par \uc2  Russian stocks await a boost in fund flows from the U.S. Federal Reserve's stimulus plan, but the market is not yet positioned for a rally, having a larger proportion of long positions, said Ivan Samokhin at Aton brokerage.\par \par \uc2  In a sign of lukewarm investor interest, market volatility and declining trading volumes in Central and Eastern Europe, including Russia, has forced Dutch bank ING to close its equity markets desk for the region.\par \par \uc2  Russian stocks have underperformed the price of oil and languish at a 50 percent valuation discount to other emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  However, stocks were supported on Monday by Russia's PMI manufacturing data showing monthly growth. \par \par \uc2  "Importantly, output growth strengthened at the end of the third quarter, signalling a still solid pace of production expansion," \uc2 Alexander Morozov\uc2 , chief economist for Russia at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , said in a note.\par \par \uc2  The data provided an argument for \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue monetary policy tightening, Morozov added. \par \par \uc2  The regulator surprised the market by raising all its key interest rates in mid-September, attracting carry trade and pushing the rouble higher.\par \par \uc2  Economists, polled by Reuters last Friday, expected rates to stay on hold in October because of slowing economic growth in Russia.\par \par \uc2  A recovery in the oil price - a key source of revenues for Russia - helped the rouble to firm. \par \par \uc2  The rouble was up 0.5 percent versus the dollar at 31.03. Overall, the rouble has gained 3.0 percent against the greenback this year, outperforming its BRIC peers.\par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed 0.3 percent to 35.11 against the euro-dollar basket. It was flat versus the euro at 40.10.\par \par \uc2  Better than expected U.S. manufacturing data eclipsed the signs of weakness in China and Brent crude futures rose 0.3 percent to $112.7 per barrel.\par \par \uc2  "In general, hope for positive trends, for central banks' stimuli, are prevailing, but the euro zone economy remains weak," said Igor Akinshin, a dealer at \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 , adding that the rouble may get stuck in the range of 34.65-35.65 against the basket, where \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Also overhanging markets is weak Chinese and euro zone manufacturing data, highlighting the frailty of the global economy and continuing uncertainty over a bail-out for Spain, whose credit rating is due for a review by Moody's Investors Service.\par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll last week showed the rouble weakening to 31.71 against the greenback by the end of 2012. On Monday non-deliverable forwards showed the rouble at 31.7890 per dollar in three months' time.\par \par \uc2  The Russian debt market was broadly flat on Monday. The yield on Russia's benchmark Eurobond maturing in 2030 fell to 2.96 percent from 2.98 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \