\par\par \b \uc2 Russia spends $1.12 bln to prop up rouble in July\b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2012\par 08:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Aug 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly halved \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July compared to the previous month and sold $1.04 billion and 69.4 million euros ($86.15 million), to ease downside pressure on the rouble, the bank said on its web site on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the rouble within a floating band, where it buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to the lower boundary and starts selling dollars and euros when the rouble weakens towards the upper boundary.\par \par \uc2  The bank widened the rouble's trading band by 100 kopecks to seven roubles in late July in a move aimed at boosting the rouble's flexibility and the efficiency of the bank's interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2 The lower boundary stands at 31.65 roubles and the upper boundary at 38.65 roubles versus the euro-dollar basket , comprised of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros.\par \par \uc2  The rouble had eased 0.15 percent to 35.08 versus the basket by 0614 GMT on Tuesday, sliding off its strongest levels since May hit overnight. ($1 = 0.8056 euros) \par \par \uc2 (Writing by Andrey Ostroukh; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | D | E | RBN | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120807e8870008s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
