\par\par \b \uc2 Falling Oil Price Cuts Short Ruble Rally\b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2012\par 14:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Falling oil prices and dashed hopes for stimulus from the U.S Federal Reserve slammed the Russian ruble Friday, reversing a four-day rally and sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 At around 12:26 GMT, the ruble traded at RUB32.81 against the dollar, a loss of 1.4% from the previous day's close. Against a basket of dollars and euros used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a broader gauge of the ruble's strength, Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was off by 1.1% to RUB36.39.\par \par \uc2 After hitting its lowest levels in more than three years Monday, the ruble reversed course as investors took profits amid growing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Global markets dipped Friday, a day after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said the regulator should see serious signs of economic deterioration before expanding current stimulus measures or introducing new ones.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices--Russia's chief export--hovered around a 16-month low of $98 per barrel, far below the estimated $117 per barrel the country needs to balance its budget.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also closing out ruble positions ahead of a four-day holiday weekend in Russia which may bring negative news on global markets. Markets will be open on Saturday before closing until Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We're expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to become active in the markets once again, but this will have little positive effect right now," ING said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia sold $70 million in the open market Thursday, cutting its support of the ruble by more than half from the $183 million sold on Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires, 7 495 232 9192; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com [ 08-06-12 1248GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120608e8680012y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
