\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Ruble Hits Three-Year Low;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Downplays Drop\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2012\par 18:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Ruble pares losses after central bankers comment on slide\par \par \uc2 --Bank of Russia Chairman Ignatyev says ruble not "doomed to fall"\par \par \uc2 --Depreciation stems from euro-zone crisis, chairman says\par \par \uc2 --Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't deviate from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, chairman says\par \par \uc2 (Updates with closing prices, additional comments.)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Russia's ruble declined to a fresh-three year low Friday on falling oil prices and fears of slowing global growth, but recovered some of its decline near the close after \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Sergei Ignatyev downplayed the depreciation as a by-product of the euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 The ruble lost as much as 1.8% to RUB34.08 per dollar, its weakest level since April 2009, as prices for Brent crude oil fell below $100 per barrel for the first time in eight months on disappointing manufacturing data from China and Europe. Traders were later encouraged by Ignatyev's comment that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ruble had already been "quite intensive" and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline would slow. The ruble pared its loss to 0.6% on the day.\par \par \uc2 "The selling had to stop at some point," said Roman Pakhomenko, a trader at Lanta bank in Moscow. "We can't just keep falling day after day."\par \par \uc2 The ruble depreciated as much as 2.8% against the dollar Thursday, though it rallied slightly near the close of trading. Last month, it was one of the world's worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , losing 12.2% against the greenback. Ignatyev blamed the ruble's weakness on one factor--the sovereign debt crisis in Europe.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately, the situation in Europe is worsening and so far, European politicians have not offered the market a program for combat ting these difficulties," Ignatyev said.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev said the ruble is not "doomed to fall," and predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide will slow, even if oil prices keep sinking. But he also stated the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to change its policy on market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of "fleeting events."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is gradually reducing its presence in the market as it moves the ruble closer to a free float, a policy that is expected to shield the economy in times of economic crisis, but also makes for greater \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. Investors have complained in recent days that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't doing enough to support the ruble, a criticism that another central banker, Deputy Chairman Sergei Shvetsov, tried to deflect.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see this as a collapse," Shvetsov told the Vedomosti newspaper. "If you look at the ruble's performance compared with that of many other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... there is not that much of a difference."\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a six-ruble-wide band against a basket of dollars and euros, purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble appreciates to upper limit of the corridor, and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the ruble approaches the band's lower edge. The band currently ranges from RUB32.15 to RUB38.15.\par \par \uc2 The ruble closed 0.6% weaker at RUB37.26 against the basket Friday, from RUB37.05 at the end of trading Thursday. The regulator typically shifts the borders of its floating corridor by five kopecks after it has exhausted a daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allotment of $500 million at the borders of the trading band, a policy Shvetsov said is still in place.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent volatility is "within the limits of our corridor," Shvetsov said. "It is pretty okay with us."\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires, 7 495 232 9192; [ 01-06-12 1647GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120601e8610012z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
