lly in all respects (or in all respects   \par                          save for payments made prior to the issuance of such  \par                          further bonds and, if applicable, the date and amount \par                          of the first payment on such further bonds) so that   \par                          the same shall be consolidated and form a single      \par                          series with such Bonds, provided that such further    \par                          issuance constitutes a qualified reopening for U.S.   \par                          federal income tax purposes.                          \par                                                                                \par Denomination             U.S.$200,000.                                         \par                                                                                \par Taxes                    Subject to certain exceptions, all payments under the \par                          Bonds will be made free and clear of any taxes imposed\par                          by the Russian Federation.                            \par                                                                                \par Governing Law            English law.                                          \par                                                                                \par No Waiver of Immunity    The Russian Federation has not waived any of its      \par                          sovereign immunity, and has not submitted to the      \par                          jurisdiction of any court, in respect of its          \par                          obligations under the Bonds.                          \par                                                                                \par Listing and Admission to Application has been made for the Bonds to be listed  \par Trading                  on the Official List and admitted to trading on the   \par                          Market.                                               \par                                                                                \par Risk Factors             Risks associated with the Bonds generally include: (1)\par                           there can be no assurance that Russia's credit       \par                          ratings will not be suspended, downgraded or          \par                          withdrawn; (2) the terms of the Bonds may be modified \par                          pursuant to their collective-action provisions; (3)   \par                           legal investment considerations may restrict certain \par                          investments; and (4) a trading market for the Bonds   \par                          may not develop, and if a market does develop, it may \par                          not be liquid.                                        \par                                                                                \par                          Risks associated with Russia generally include: (1)   \par                           any material reduction in the price of crude oil or  \par                          natural gas may materially and adversely affect the   \par                          revenues and financial condition of the Russian       \par                          Federation; (2) the Russian Federation's economy, like\par                          many economies, is vulnerable to external shocks, and \par                          a global economic crisis, significant future economic \par                          difficulties of the Russian Federation's major trading\par                          partners, and more general "contagion" effects all    \par                          could have a material adverse effect on the Russian   \par                          Federation's economic growth and the market for the   \par                          Bonds; (3) Russia is a foreign sovereign state, has   \par      