venue in 2011 of 11,780 billion roubles, or 20.1% of GDP and total expenditure of 12,656 billion roubles, or 21.6% of GDP. Debt service costs account for 0.7% of GDP under the 2012 budget law.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par The 2012 budget law provides for a fiscal deficit in 2012 of 877 billion\par roubles, or 1.5% of GDP, and a primary deficit in 2012 of 488 billion roubles,\par or 0.8% of GDP. According to the 2012 budget law, the Government intends to\par seek gross external borrowing in 2012 of 210 billion roubles, or 0.4% of GDP,\par and gross domestic financing of 1,809 billion roubles, or 3.1% of GDP.\par \par In 2012, 2013 and 2014, the Government expects to finance the federal deficit\par mainly through domestic and external borrowing and privatisation sales. The\par Government also expects in 2012-2014 to make drawdowns on the National Wealth\par Fund for the purpose of co-financing pensions.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Budget Revenue\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par The following table sets forth information regarding federal budget revenue for\par the periods indicated:\par \par                            Federal Budget Revenue(1)                           \par \par                       For the                                                     \par                     year ended                                                    \par                     31 December                                                   \par                                                                                   \par                         2007       2008      2009      2010       2011            \par                                                                                   \par                      (millions                                                    \par                     of roubles)                                                   \par                                                                                   \par Tota