ebt statistics of the Government.\par \par The provision of state guarantees is strictly regulated by the budget laws of\par the Russian Federation. State guarantees are provided solely on the basis of a\par Government resolution or international agreement and the budget code and\par federal budget law together with its implementating resolutions for a\par particular year and particular target period. The 2012 Budget Law provides for\par the issuance of state guarantees in support of investment projects (up to\par U.S.$1 billion in each of 2012 and 2013), the export of industrial products (up\par to U.S.$1.5 billion in each of 2012 and 2013 and up to U.S.$1.6 billion in\par 2014) and other projects with the participation of international financial\par institutions (up to U.S.$500 million in 2012, U.S.$1.3 billion in 2013 and up\par to U.S.$1.6 billion in 2014).\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Government has paid in full all of the debt service due on borrowings contracted by the Government since 1 January 1992.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Domestic Debt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table sets forth information with respect to Russia's domestic debt as of the indicated dates:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par                   Domestic Debt of the Federal Government(1)                   \par \par                      As of                                                        \par                   31 December                                                     \par                                                                                   \par                       2006      2007    2008    2009    2010    2011              \par                                                                                   \par                    (billions                                                      \par                   of roubles)                                                     \par                                                                     