\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  cbank sees March  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  at Feb levels\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 07:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects its purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March will be close to February levels, Interfax news agency quoted its First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev as saying on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The regulator bought around $2.8 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February to limit the excess strengthening in the rouble.\par \par \uc2 It keeps the rouble in a floating band against the euro-dollar basket, comprised of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros, which last stood at 32.20-38.20 roubles per basket.\par \par \uc2 Interfax also quoted Ulyukayev as saying that the band remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The bank buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rouble closes in on the lower boundary of the corridor, starts selling dollars and euros from reserves when the rouble is closer to the upper boundary, and does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the middle of the range.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Maria Kiselyova; Editing by John Bowker)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120316e83g000bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
