\par\par \b \uc2 Russian markets -- Factors to Watch on Feb 24\b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2012\par 06:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Here are events and news stories that could move Russian markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 You can reach us on: +7 495 775 1242\par \par \uc2 STOCKS CALL (Contributions to moscow.newsroom@reuters.com):\par \par \uc2 PROMSVYAZBANK: Says external factors such as the rise in US stock indexes are mildly positive for the Russian stock market;\par \par \uc2 ALOR: "Thanks to external factors, MICEX index may return to the levels of around 1560 points."\par \par \uc2 EVENTS (All times GMT):\par \par \uc2 SAROV, Russia - Prime Minister Vladimir Putin visits Sarov;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Mail.ru trading update and conference call;\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - \uc2 Nord Gold\uc2  2011 earnings;\par \par \uc2 IN THE PAPERS :\par \par \uc2 TNK-BP\uc2 , Russia's third largest crude producer, may stop its Ukrainian Lisichansk oil refinery next month as it is not profitable any more, Kommersant daily said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Russia's top lender \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  plans to sell mid-sized food retailer Vester, in which it holds a 51 percent stake following a debt restructuring in 2009, with offers already sent to O'Key and Dixy, Kommersant reports.\par \par \uc2 VTB needs long-term and cheap funds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , otherwise Russia's second largest bank will not grow and boost lending, Vedomosti daily said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Swiss-based trader Gunvor plans to build an oil terminal in the Gulf of Guinea, its first foreign terminal, Vedomosti said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      \tab \par      TOP STORIES IN RUSSIA AND THE CIS :\tab \par TOP NEWS: \par Seeking presidency, Putin evokes 1812            \tab \par TAKE-A-LOOK: Russia's presidential election         \tab \par Th