\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Sold $600M Jan  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Interventions \highlight\uc2  -Central Banker\b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2012\par 10:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds further details on bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , inflation; quotes; background.)\par \par \uc2 By Ira Iosebashvili\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $600 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this month in a bid to support the ruble, First Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "In this way we have sterilized around 18 billion to 19 billion rubles from our money supply," Ulyukayev said.\par \par \uc2 The ruble has been under pressure because of a exodus of foreign capital--amid political concerns at home and the broader euro-zone debt crisis--with almost $38 billion leaving the country in the fourth quarter alone, the largest quarterly outflows since the 2008 financial crisis. Capital flight totaled $84.2 billion in 2011 compared with $33.6 billion in 2010, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 Markets and investors were concerned over the outcome of parliamentary elections in December and the waves of protests that greeted the results and are keeping an eye on coming presidential election in March.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for years has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the ruble in a targeted range against the euro and the dollar. On Dec. 27, the bank expanded that range to allow for greater daily fluctuations as part of continuing efforts to transition to a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something Ulyukayev said Russia had "practically" achieved.\par \par \uc2 He said that inflation--which finished 2011 at a post-Soviet Union low of 6.1% and stands in January at 4.8% compared with the year-earlier period--is at historically low levels because of a favorable comparison with last year's data and falling consumer product prices, which are likely to continue falling until April or May of this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts inflation of 5%-6% in 2012.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232-9192; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 19, 2012 04:19 ET (09:19 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120119e81j002kr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
