\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia c.bank says eases  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  support despite outflows\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2012\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank sold $600 mln roubles so far in Jan to support rouble\par \par \uc2 * Sold $1.773 billion and 191.7 million euros in December\par \par \uc2 * Sees inflation at below 1 percent in January\par \par \uc2 * Says capital outflow "seemingly" continued\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)\par \par \uc2 By Darya Korsunskaya and Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it had scaled down its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January even though the rouble remains under pressure from capital leaving the country.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent $600 million so far this month to support the rouble, First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said. This compares with $1.8 billion and 192 million euros ($246 million) spent on supporting the rouble in December.\par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev would not say how much capital has left the country since the beginning of the year, saying only the outflows "seemingly" continued as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A net total of $84.2 billion left the country in 2011 with capital flight accelerating in to $37.8 billion the last quarter, when protests broke out over alleged ballot fraud in December's parliamentary election.\par \par \uc2 The large scale of the protests, unprecedented in Prime Minister Vladimir Putin's 12-year rule, has unsettled investors even though no credible rival has emerged to challenge his bid to return to the Kremlin in a March presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev said the bank will continue controlling money supply dynamics, as it aims to keep full-year inflation at 5-6 percent after inflation eased to a record post-Soviet low of 6.1 percent in 2011 thanks to an exceptionally good harvest that pushed foodstuff prices down and moderating money supply growth.\par \par \uc2 January's month-on-month inflation rate will come in at "significantly less than 1 (percent)," Ulyukayev told reporters on the sidelines of an economic conference hosted by a liberal economic think tank founded by late premier Yegor Gaidar.\par \par \uc2 Year-on-year inflation growth could slow to below 5 percent in coming months until May but in the longer term underlying inflationary risks remain, Ulyukayev said.\par \par \uc2 Inflation figures are being flattered by the postponement of annual hikes in household utility bills - a move widely seen as an attempt to woo voters ahead of the March presidential poll.\par \par \uc2 Weekly CPI readings are running at just 0.1 percent and the Economy Ministry expects year-on-year inflation to fall this month to a post-Soviet low of 4.8 percent from the end-2011 reading of 6.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 INFLATION TARGETING\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also continues its transition from controlling the exchange rate as its main monetary tool to targeting inflation instead, Ulyukayev said. But the bank still keeps the rouble within a range against a target euro-dollar basket and sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rouble weakens towards the lower boundary of the corridor.\par \par \uc2 The bank starts buying dollars and euros when the rouble approaches the top end of the band, which last stood at 32.20-38.20, and does not carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the middle of the corridor.\par \par \uc2 "The free float (of the rouble) is almost achieved... Supply and demand on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are seen now where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not carrying out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ulyukayev said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the rouble traded flat at 31.5 against the dollar and at 35.58 versus the dollar-euro basket .\par \par \uc2 'OPTIMAL' RATES CORRIDOR\par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev also said that the size of the current interest rate corridor "is close to optimal. I think that for now, it is at a level comfortable for the regulator (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), market participants."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark refinancing rate now stands at 8 percent, while its deposit rate is at 4 percent, and the International Monetary Fund has urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on numerous occasions to tighten the band further.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; writing by Vladimir Soldatkin; Editing by Douglas Busvine/Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120122e81j00057\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
