\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bank Of Russia Widens Ruble's Trading Corridor Vs Basket\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2011\par 16:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2011 10:07 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia Widens Ruble Trading Corridor To 6 Rubles From 5 Rubles\par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2011 10:10 EDT *DJ  Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Lowers \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Threshold To $500 Mln From $600 Mln\par \par \uc2 27 Dec 2011 10:24 EDT DJ  Bank Of Russia Widens Ruble's Trading Corridor\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the ruble's trading band versus a basket of dollars and euros, while lowering the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it will conduct before moving the corridor's boundaries, the regulator said in a statement Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's trading band was widened to six rubles from five rubles as of Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. At the same time, the regulator will now shift the borders of the basket's corridor after buying or selling $500 million worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The previous amount for a trading band shift was $600 million.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia manages the ruble in a trading band versus a basket of dollars and euros, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble strengthens, selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ruble when it weakens, and doing nothing when the ruble is in the middle of the band.\par \par \uc2 "Raising the potential flexibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate through these changes will help the effectiveness of monetary policy used by the Bank of Russia to maintain price stability," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232-9192; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 27, 2011 10:24 ET (15:24 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111227e7cr002wq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
