\par\par \b \uc2 Russia spent $9.2 bln to boost rouble since early Sept\b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2011\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $8 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month and some $1.15 on Tuesday to keep the rouble from excessive weakening, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Sergei Ignatyev said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the rouble in a floating band versus the euro-dollar basket and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it deems necessary to prevent excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate.\par \par \uc2 "(On Tuesday) we sold more than usually, $1.15 billion," Ignatyev told journalists.\par \par \uc2 "In whole September (we sold) around $8 billion."\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev also said that the regulator has not changed the forecast for 2011 capital outflows. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's estimates that net capital outflows will reach around $35 billion this year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Darya Korsunskaya; Writing by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Andrey Ostroukh)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -C.BANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111005e7a5000al\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
