\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Ruble Hits Lowest Level Since Aug 2009 On Oil, Europe Fears\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2011\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, comment.)\par \par \uc2 By Ira Iosebashvili\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble hit its weakest level versus the dollar since August 2009 on Tuesday, as Europe's debt woes worsened and oil prices slipped toward levels thought to be critical for Russia's markets.\par \par \uc2 "The level of negativity on markets has grown, and headlining once again is the news from Europe," \uc2 Gazprombank\uc2  said in a note to investors.\par \par \uc2 Greece said Monday its budget deficit would be greater than forecast. On Sunday, the cash-strapped country said it would miss 2011 targets set by the European Union and International Monetary Fund as a prerequisite for receiving aid.\par \par \uc2 Fears of a fresh banking crisis in Europe triggered a flight of capital out of emerging markets, dragging the ruble to as low as RUB32.75 versus the dollar on Tuesday, a loss of 0.5% and its lowest level in 25-months. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 0.3% against a basket of dollars and euros to RUB37.46, not far from the RUB37.55 level that is expected to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark Micex index was down 2.4% at 1312.60 by 0840 GMT after starting the day with gains. The ruble-denominated RTS fell below 1260, its lowest point since May 2010.\par \par \uc2 Prices for oil--Russia's chief export--tumbled nearly 1% to below $101 a barrel for Brent crude, approaching levels traders say are critical for Russian markets.\par \par \uc2 "The $100 per barrel level is being watched very closely," said Alexei Borichev, a trader at ING in London. "If Brent breaks below $100 and stays there for more than a few days, investors will start leaving Russia in droves and traders will increase their bets against the ruble and stocks. It will trigger a very negative situation."\par \par \uc2 Corporate debt repayments may be causing additional pressure on the ruble, traders said. Russian banks and companies are scheduled to pay out some $38 billion in debt by year-end, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232-9195; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com [ 04-10-11 0900GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111004e7a4000nk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
