\par\par \b \uc2 Eastern Europe Steps Up  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 19:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Poland sending strong message to the market as it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  for third consecutive trading day\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the Leu\par \par \uc2 LONDON -- Authorities in Eastern Europe cranked up their efforts to prop up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, as Poland \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third consecutive trading day and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  also piled in to support the ruble.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought its domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro, while the Bank of Russia is suspected of selling at least $400 million, as well as shifting its trading band--which it uses to contain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility--five kopeks weaker, after news that Greece would miss its deficit targets this year triggered another sell-off in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, according to one dealer as central banks in emerging markets step in to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, which can pose inflationary problems, by lifting the cost of imported goods.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, for those countries burdened with large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debt, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness is particularly harmful as these debts become much more expensive to pay back.\par \par \uc2 That is especially the case for Poland, whose \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up its fight Monday to defend the zloty, something for which it has more than enough reserves to do, market participants say.\par \par \uc2 "The National Bank of Poland has enough ammunition with its $100 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to stay in the game for some time and [it] could be successful," said Murat Toprak, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 That being said, the job won't be easy.\par \par \uc2 "It will be very difficult for the Polish authorities to reverse the trend because foreign investors will use the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to scale down long positions in Polish bonds," said Bartosz Pawlowski, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate strategy for the Central and Eastern Europe, Middle East and Africa region for \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in London.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, Latin America, Eastern Europe and Africa have been under heavy selling pressure in recent weeks as a toxic combination of global economy fears and escalating euro-zone debt worries led investors to fold their bets in emerging markets on a colossal scale.\par \par \uc2 Greece concerns ramped up that pressure Monday forcing central banks in the region into action again. The trading band of the ruble against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket now spans 32.55 to 37.55, said Mikhail Anisimov, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at VTB Capital in Moscow. That comes after the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $2.36 billion defending the ruble, believed to be the biggest one-day dollar sale by the regulator since the financial crisis and oil-price decline that started in 2008.\par \par \uc2 At 1558 GMT the euro was trading at RON4.315 against the Romanian leu, down around 1% on the day. Against the Polish zloty, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at PLN4.3868, down from session highs hit earlier of PLN4.4401.\par \par \uc2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 94966; clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Katie Martin in London and William Mauldin in Moscow contributed to this item) [ 10-03-11 1315ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111003e7a30005g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
