\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Of Russia Ruble Trade Band Shifts 5 Kopeks Weaker - Banker\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 12:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Russia's trading band used to contain the volatility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have shifted 5 kopeks weaker, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably sold at least $400 million on Monday to support the ruble, bankers said Monday.\par \par \uc2 The trading band of the ruble against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket now spans 32.55 to 37.55, said Mikhail Anisimov, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at VTB Capital in Moscow. The ruble weakened against the basket to slightly beyond 37.50 on the Micex exchange Monday and then subsequently strengthened a bit to 37.36 to the dollar-euro basket.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, but Chairman Sergei Ignatiev said last week the trading band spanned 32.50 to 37.50. The ruble dropped to 32.53 against the dollar on Monday. Brent crude sank 1% to $101.73 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Anisimov said there appeared to be two-way order traffic on the ruble on Monday, with ruble-selling by hedge funds counteracted by purchases from Russian exporters of various sectors. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably sold $400 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 Gazprombank\uc2  analyst Anna Bogdyukevich said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has definitely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is too early to tell how much money they have spent, perhaps $600 million. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, using a formula that depends on the ruble's level in the trading band.\par \par \uc2 Natlia Orlova, economist at \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 , said the ruble trading band's edge is now probably 37.55 or 37.60, and the Bank of Russia may have sold about $1 billion.\par \par \uc2 A week earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $2.36 billion defending the ruble, believed to be the biggest one-day dollar sale by the regulator since the financial crisis and oil-price decline that started in 2008.\par \par \uc2 -By William Mauldin, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232-9192, william.mauldin@dowjones.com [ 03-10-11 1038GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111003e7a3000r5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
