\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ(9/28) Moscow Moves To Calm Investors\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2011\par 02:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par A11\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (From THE WALL STREET JOURNAL) \par    By William Mauldin and Alexander Kolyandr \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW -- Top Russian officials sought to reassure investors alarmed by the sudden removal of long-serving Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin, predicting a rebound for the ruble even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it spent $2.36 billion on Monday to shore up the slumping \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund, meanwhile, warned that heavy government spending could threaten Russia's economic stability if global conditions worsen. The IMF echoed Mr. Kudrin's own concerns, which precipitated his ouster on Monday by President Dmitry Medvedev after the minister voiced them publicly over the weekend.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Sergei Ignatiev called a rare media briefing to talk up the ruble's prospects Tuesday, saying the bank wouldn't widen its target band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "If the current level of oil prices holds, the probability of the ruble strengthening in the coming weeks is much higher than of its weakening," he said.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin economic aide Arkady Dvorkovich chimed in later on Twitter, praising Mr. Ignatiev's comments, adding, "The authorities have everything necessary to maintain stability."\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Ignatiev also acknowledged the downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been battered as global investors have fled assets seen as risky in recent weeks. Mr. Ignatiev said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent over $6 billion this month to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline, including the more than $2 billion on Monday. Traders said Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the largest since the financial crisis led \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to let the ruble drop sharply in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worked at least temporarily, and the ruble strengthened to 31.69 per dollar on the Micex exchange, compared with 32.42 late Monday. Mr. Ignatiev blamed the weak ruble on capital flight due to global market turmoil. It was unclear whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more rubles on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 But the IMF and Mr. Kudrin said many of Russia's financial woes lie closer to home.\par \par \uc2 In his first public statement since he was removed Monday by Mr. Medvedev for publicly criticizing the government's plans for big increases in defense and social spending, Mr. Kudrin stood by his critique.\par \par \uc2 "For the past several months, despite my numerous objections, some of them made publicly, decisions were taken on budget policies that without doubt have increased budget risks," he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kudrin, viewed by many investors as a bulwark of Russia's financial stability in his 12 years in office, said he first tried to quit over the issue in February, but Prime Minister Vladimir Putin convinced him to stay on. "Budget risks are connected first of all with excessive commitments in the defense sector and social sector that will inevitably affect the entire national economy," he said.\par \par \uc2 In a regular report on Russia, meanwhile, the IMF warned that surging spending has left the country vulnerable to a drop in prices for its main export, oil.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 27, 2011 20:17 ET (00:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110928e79s0003y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
