\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: Russia Cuts Rate On Global Economic Picture - Aton\b0\par\par\uc2 1,170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2011\par 11:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0905 GMT [Dow Jones] Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reduced its repo rate to address concerns about liquidity stemming from the global economic outlook rather than problems in the local banking system, Aton strategist Peter Westin says. Ruble weakens slightly after the rate decision, to 30.37 to the dollar from 30.31. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0904 GMT [Dow Jones] The Bank of Russia moved to cut its repo rate to address seasonal liquidity problems, \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  economist Julia Tsepliaeva says. "The second half of September and October are typical periods of poorer ruble liquidity with repo rates to become crucial," Tsepliaeva says. Ruble weakens slightly after the rate decision, to 30.37 to the dollar from 30.31. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0903 GMT [Dow Jones] HUF eases further against EUR amid worries that Hungarian policy would hurt the banking system and the economy and amid renewed euro zone woes after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgraded two French banks. EUR/HUF is at 286.49, vs 286.20 early Wednesday and versus 283.89 late Tuesday. Raiffeisen Bank expects to see EUR/HUF trading in the 283.40-286.35 range Wednesday and EUR/HUF at 285 by year-end. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0902 GMT [Dow Jones] Russia's rate move is aimed at cutting volatility, ING says, commenting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut the repo rate by 25 bps while at the same time raising the deposit rate by 25 bps. By cutting the spread between the repo rate, which provides liquidity, and the deposit rate, which absorbs it, the Bank of Russia gives money market rates a narrower corridor to bounce around in and increases the effectiveness of its policies, ING explains. The hike in the deposit rate may also be a reaction to weakness in the ruble, which has weakened nearly 9% since the beginning of August, ING says. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT [Dow Jones] RUB may fall as Russia targets rates, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says, commenting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut the repo rate by 25 bps while at the same time raising the deposit rate by 25 bps. "They are taking another step toward rate targeting, which means that they will have to take a step away from managing the ruble, since a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot to both at once," says Alexander Morozov, chief economist HSBC \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That would mean either less \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility, or a widening of the ruble's trading corridor, and "since the recent trend in the ruble has been one of weakening, this could ensure that the ruble weakens even faster, without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up," Morozov says. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0858 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds oscillate between positive and negative territory. Bunds had opened higher after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cut the debt ratings of \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  and \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 , but renewed chatter of China's support for peripheral euro-zone bonds helped stocks off their lows, in turn pulling bunds down. Results of the schatz auction will be out around 0915 GMT and, apart from that, traders will take cues from any comments on the euro-zone debt situation. December bunds are down 0.05 at 137.69.(neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0858 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/THB turns higher at 30.27 from 30.20 late Tuesday, tracking broad USD strength against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors are in risk-off mode amid growing concerns over euro-zone sovereign debt woes and European banks' financial health. Exporters' dollar-selling demand helps take the pair off the day's high of 30.31. "Capital outflows are seen across the region and I guess that such outflows from Thailand would mainly come from the bond market," says a dealer at a local bank. "The dollar/baht is heading toward the 30.30 resistance level and it's likely to break through that level tomorrow," he adds. The pair's support is pegged at 30.17. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0857 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are little changed after UK labor data which came in better than expected. Jobless claims rose by 20,300 in August vs expectations for an increase of 35,000. Despite this, gilts are continuing their recent outperformance vs bunds. December gilts are up 0.14 at 130.67. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0852 GMT [Dow Jones] European sovereign CDS tighten except for Greece, as a short-covering rally overrides the French bank downgrades and caution ahead of the conference call later this afternoon between the Greek prime minister and the French and German leaders. Markit notes Greece is trading 57.5 bps upfront, 1.5 bps wider on the day. Adds Italy is 27 bps tighter at 480 bps, Spain is 18 bps tighter at 405 bps, Portugal is 27 bps tighter at 1170 bps, Ireland is 24 bps tighter at 870 bps. (art.patnaude@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0850 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  sees a muted Swiss CPI threat from SNB move and with August consumer prices rising just 0.2% on the year, the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can maintain its 1.20 franc per euro cap "for years" without endangering price stability, says \uc2 UBS\uc2 . "Clearly, there is a risk inflation can increase faster if Switzerland's economy expands more than anticipated in 2012 and 2013, but global growth remains weak, and the the SNB could maintain its new policy stance for years, just as it did in the late 1970s," according to chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mansoor Mohi-uddin. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0848 GMT [Dow Jones] Belgium bonds may edge toward Spain says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . If Belgium should fail to form a permanent government, Belgian OLOs, could drift "much closer" toward Spanish government bond levels, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . Bond supply is scheduled for September 26. Belgium's caretaker Prime Minister Yves Leterme Tuesday announced a bid to run for deputy chief of the OECD. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0848 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors still seek safety in USD, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 , with JPY, CHF no longer filling this role, and EUR out of the competition for now. Says despite the possibility of a US default and the Fed's expansionary monetary policy, investors looking for security in the G-10 universe have no other choice. Warns that both NOK and AUD, which would be alternatives from a fundamental point of view, have in the past suffered when sentiment sours. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is painfully slow at ending old habits. As a result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have previously reacted to rising risk aversion, will remain under pressure, while the greenback is able to appreciate," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. EUR/USD is at 1.3653. (jessica.mead@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 14, 2011 05:05 ET (09:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110914e79e00273\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
