\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: RUB May Fall As Russia Targets Rates - \uc2 HSBC\b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2011\par 10:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0859 GMT [Dow Jones] RUB may fall as Russia targets rates, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says, commenting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut the repo rate by 25 bps while at the same time raising the deposit rate by 25 bps. "They are taking another step toward rate targeting, which means that they will have to take a step away from managing the ruble, since a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot to both at once," says Alexander Morozov, chief economist HSBC \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That would mean either less \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility, or a widening of the ruble's trading corridor, and "since the recent trend in the ruble has been one of weakening, this could ensure that the ruble weakens even faster, without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up," Morozov says. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 14-09-11 0859GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110914e79e000pw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
