\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia stock, rouble fall after US payrolls\b0\par\par\uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2011\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Stocks down on poor U.S. payrolls data\par \par \uc2 * Rouble eases across board, to extend loss next week-dealer\par \par \uc2 * Strong oil, dollar sales prevent rouble from deeper fall\par \par \uc2 (Adds reaction to US data, quotes, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Nastassia Astrasheuskaya\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 2 (Reuters) - Russian stocks and the rouble weakened on \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday, tracking falls on major stock markets a  fter  key U.S.\par employment data  failed to meet analysts' growth forecast. \tab \par  The U.S. August non-farm payrolls came in flat in the lowest reading since\par last September, U.S. Labor Department data showed, while analysts had forecast a\par 75,000 increase. \tab \par   The stagnating U.S. job market, which keeps pressure on the Federal Reserve\par to provide more monetary stimulus to aid the world's top economy, sent global\par markets down and investors out of assets such as oil and into gold \par , a traditional hedge against inflation.\tab \par   By  1422 GMT, the dollar-based RTS index and\par the rouble  -  traded MICEX had lost 2.6 percent and 2.3\par percent respectively to reach their week lows , underperforming the broader\par emerging markets index , which was down   1.5  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Given the recent market volatility, today's U.S. statistics-driven fall is nothing extraordinary. It's not a collapse, by today's standards it's a normal market reaction to poor macro data," said Vladimir Bragin, analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Next, the market will be watching the Federal Reserve's reaction to today's data, which is quite a stimulus for a third round of quantitative easing," Bragin added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROUBLE RESISTS DEEP FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Oil prices  , although down more than 2 percent in Brent\par crude futures to below $112 per barrel <LCOc1> ,  remained\par  strong enough to curb the  rouble  's\par losses,  keeping it around  29.  10 against the\par dollar   , down  \par 0.  34  percent  , compared to a 0.2  \par  percent morning fall. \tab \par  V  ersus the euro  , the rouble extended losses to\par  41.  47, losing 0.48 percent  \par  , as the s  hared  European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par climbed to  a  session high against the greenback after\par the U.S. employment data  . \tab \par  Analysts at Renaissance Capital say a further oil price fall\par may lead to a "s  hort-term weakness in the rouble towards\par 31  .00  -32  .00 per dollar," also  \par reducing  share prices  for Russian energy\par names  . \tab \par  Versus the euro-dollar basket, used by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to guide\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's nominal exchange rate, the rouble lost\par 0.  4  percent to 34.  67   .\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The rouble fell against the basket on the general external negativity which hung above the markets throughout the day, while weak U.S. employment statistics accelerated the fall," said Victor Anisimov, dealer at Aljba-Alliance bank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Friday effect, when investors want to sell and leave the market, and exporters' dollar sales, prevented the rouble from an even deeper fall," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Anisimov expects the rouble to extend its fall to 34.70 versus the basket at Monday's opening, which would still be in the range of 34.15-35.15, within which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed not to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought a relatively modest amount of $0.5 billion in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month, First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said on Friday. The small size of the dollar buying was further evidence that the bank has shifted towards greater exchange-rate flexibility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ulyukayev also said last month's market turmoil would not lead to a policy shift in Russia; adding to signs that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hold rates at its next monthly policy meeting after Brazil surprisingly cut rates this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The spread on Russia's dollar bonds over comparable U.S. securities expanded to 25 5 basis points after the U.S. macro data\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from below 240 in the previous session . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Russia's 30-year benchmark Eurobond's yield increased  to\par 4.1  2  percent , staying away from the 2011 low of 4.04\par seen a month ago. \tab \par \tab \par Russian                            Latest      Net       %    Change \par Markets                                      Change  Change   on year\par       Stocks                                                       \par MICEX                      1515.52    -36.06   -2.32   -10.22 \par RTS                       1657.79    -46.07   -2.70    -7.99 \par London ADRs              914.69    -27.69   -2.94    -7.40 \par Emrg Mkt Indx           1022.90    -15.10   -1.45   -11.16 \par MSCI Russia        303.01     -6.02   -1.95    -8.36 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2                 82.47     -2.62   -3.08   -20.84 \par VTB                        0.07     -0.00   -2.49   -26.34 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2                   171.52     -5.83   -3.29   -11.36 \par LUKOIL             