\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia stocks rise, rouble weakens after Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2011\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Aug 26 (Reuters) - * Rouble flat, retains support from oil and tax payments\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Aug 26 (Reuters) - Russian stock markets entered positive territory ahead of the weekend, tracking global peers and oil prices as investors still held out hope that the Federal Reserve may eventually provide a boost to the ailing US economy.\par \par \uc2 Fed chairman Ben Bernanke on Friday stopped short of signalling further actions to boost the world's largest economy, but added the Fed is prepared to use its own tools to spur growth if needed.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets fell at first but then headed north, with the dollar-based RTS index adding 0.77 percent in the main trading session to 1,596.2 points, while the rouble-traded MICEX\par \par \uc2 index finished the day up 1.1 percent at 1,458.8 points.\par \par \uc2 "Russian speculators are tired of pricing in moves on the U.S. market because of too strong volatility. Only a few players now are ready to bet on where the American market will close today," said Mikhail Kozakov at Grandis Capital brokerage.\par \par \uc2 "Generally Bernanke has provided a hope that the Fed will offer something new. People are not going to sell everything -- they prefer to wait and understand what Bernanke meant," said Kozakov.\par \par \uc2 The Russian market got support from oil prices, its traditional driver, that climbed above $110 per barrel, ensuring fresh inflows of dollars and euros into the export-focused economy.\par \par \uc2 The rouble gave up earlier gains, ending the session virtually unchanged at 28.95 per dollar and easing 0.1 percent to 41.57 against the euro .\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro-dollar basket, the rouble was at 34.62\par \par \uc2 , remaining in the range of 34.15-35.15 that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed not to require \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to be supported by month-end tax payments, with around 200 billion roubles ($6.9 billion) to be paid in income taxes by Monday, as export-focused companies usually convert dollar revenues to meet local liabilities.\par \par \uc2 The spread on Russia's dollar bonds over comparable U.S. securities remained steady at 254 points, reflecting a substantial premium to the average emerging market index reading of 339, according to \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's EMBI+ debt indexes . ($1 = 28.945 Russian Roubles)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Andrey Ostroukh and Vladimir Abramov, Editing by Douglas Busvine and Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110826e78q000j6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
