\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian stocks, rouble rise on stronger oil\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 11 (Reuters) - * RTS, MICEX recover some of recent losses\par \par \uc2 * Rouble firms on supportive oil, cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  GDP figures add to negative sentiment\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Aug 11 (Reuters) - Russian stocks ended higher on Thursday's after seven days of losses, while the rouble firmed on the back of recovery in oil prices and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market mood improved after data showed the number of Americans claiming new jobless benefits dropped to a four-month low last week, but market players say it will take a long time for the market to recover to levels seen before the U.S. sovereign rating downgrade.\par \par \uc2 "Generally, the situation now is like during the crisis of 2008 apart from the fact that there is much more liquidity," said Alexei Surov at Zenit bank.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark RTS index rose 0.5 percent to 1,544.83 points in the main session, rebounding from its lowest level since early October 2010 of 1,510.72 hit earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 At one stage in mid-afternoon it was down more than 4 percent, demonstrating the extent of recent volatility.\par \par \uc2 The rouble-traded MICEX added 0.52 percent to 1,438.91 points, finishing the session far below levels of around 1,740 points seen in the beginning August.\par \par \uc2 "The market is still oversold and such a situation can last for several more days," said Surov.\par \par \uc2 However it may be premature to "buy on dips" now because the Russian stock market could drop another 20-25 percent, said Peter Westin, strategist at investment group Aton, which manages 13 billion roubles ($458.5 million) in Russian and foreign assets.\par \par \uc2 ROUBLE REGAINS STRENGTH\par \par \uc2 The rouble firmed, recording gains against the euro, the dollar and the euro-dollar basket -- the measure the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The rouble strengthened 0.36 percent to 42.03 versus the euro , 0.95 percent against the dollar to 29.47\par \par \uc2 and 0.64 percent to 35.13 versus the basket\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The situation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remains restless although the rouble shows some success thanks to more expensive oil," said Dmitry Kharlampiev, an analyst at Petrocommerce bank.\par \par \uc2 Although Brent crude <LCOc1> slipped on Thursday, reversing the previous session's gain of 4 percent, it still remained comfortable for Russia's budget at 106.8 per barrel .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also propped up the rouble by frequently selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent sharp drops in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "The external background will be the number one (factor) and the basket's attempts to rise could not be excluded," Kharlampiev said.\par \par \uc2 Investors' attitude towards Russia and its assets may have been also affected by weak economic data that showed that gross domestic product grew 3.4 percent in the second quarter compared to the economy ministry forecast of 3.7 percent.\par \par \uc2 "In spite of high oil prices of around $115 per barrel in the first half of 2011, the Russian recovery has been deeply disappointing and has lagged well behind its emerging market peers," analysts at Capital Economics said in a note.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh, Zlata Garasyuta and Vladimir Abramov; editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110811e78b000rm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
