\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Not Stopping RUB Decline - Banks\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2011\par 15:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not been enough to slow the falling ruble, which Tuesday saw its biggest drop ever against a basket of dollars and euro, market players said.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars already in small amounts of $150 million to $200 million per day above RUB35.20 against the basket. However, this is not sufficient if the bank is to stem the decline in the ruble," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Spurred by commodity prices crumbling in the face of slowing global growth and a downgrade of the U.S. debt rating, Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell by as much as 4% against the basket to RUB35.93, its largest drop since the instrument was created by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2005. The drop comes amid steep declines in the ruble compared with the dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia keeps its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a five-ruble wide trading corridor, which currently stands at 32.25 to 37.25 against the basket, market players estimate. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollars when the ruble moves towards the weaker end of the corridor, buys dollars when the ruble moves towards the stronger end, and does nothing when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stays in the one ruble-wide zone in the middle of the band.\par \par \uc2 It's clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is present in the market, "but the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been hard to pinpoint because of its new, more flexible policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trader at a large Russian bank said. "Whatever they are doing is clearly not enough to make a difference."\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232 9195; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com [ 09-08-11 1335GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110809e789001bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
