\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Russia's rouble and monetary policy\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 17:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged on Thursday, steering a cautious path between supporting economic growth and keeping inflation in check.\par \par \uc2 For a full story on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision, click on:\par \par \uc2 Following is a run-down of Russian monetary policy:\par \par \uc2 ROUBLE BASKET\par \par \uc2 Russia introduced a basket for tracking the rouble in February 2005, initially consisting of 0.1 euros to 0.9 dollars. The euro's share was gradually increased and since February 2007 the basket has consisted of 0.45 euros to 0.55 dollars.\par \par \uc2 FLOATING CORRIDOR\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a floating rouble corridor in early 2010, shifting its boundaries up or down by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the upper or lower boundary.\par \par \uc2 Between mid-February and mid-May 2010 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made 32 such shifts, bringing the corridor to 33.40-36.40 roubles against the basket.\par \par \uc2 On Oct. 13, 2010, Russia widened the corridor symmetrically to 4 roubles from 3, and decreased the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  necessary for band shifts to $650 million.\par \par \uc2 From March 1, 2011, the band was widened further to 5 roubles, while the size of cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  which prompt a shift in boundaries was reduced to $600 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to decide on the next band widening in autumn, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Chairman Sergei Shvetsov told Reuters in an interview . He also said that the mechanism of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself has not changed in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are based on any foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales or purchases in excess of the so-called daily 'target' volumes set at each month-end based on estimates of the budget balance, Finance Ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and oil price. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not disclose these daily limits.\par \par \uc2 The corridor now stands at 32.25-37.25 roubles versus the basket, according to market players' assessments.\par \par \uc2 The floating corridor itself is split into three.\par \par \uc2 When the rouble is at the weak end of the corridor, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells small volumes of dollars each day. In the one-rouble wide corridor in the middle of the band it does nothing. When the rouble is strong it buys dollars and euros.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  increase as the rouble approaches the corridor's boundaries, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing the size of its bid on the market, meaning the amount needed to shift the band is accumulated more quickly. The daily limit on planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, remains unchanged.\par \par \uc2 A wider, fixed-trading band of 26 to 41 roubles was introduced in January 2009 and scrapped in October 2010.\par \par \uc2 MOVE TOWARDS 'DIRTY' FREE FLOAT\par \par \uc2 Russia is gradually moving towards targeting inflation rather than exchange rates, often declaring its readiness to promote the rouble to the status of a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it is aiming for a managed -- or 'dirty' -- free float and will continue to reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it deems it necessary.\par \par \uc2 Gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves -- at their highest level since October 2008, and at $535 billion and the world's third largest -- give \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The regulator says it does not target a particular exchange rate, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are merely aimed at smoothing out excessive market volatility.\par \par \uc2 By moving away from a controlled rate policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been increasing the role of its interest rate policy.\par \par \uc2 At its last meeting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the refinancing rate at 8.25 percent and the deposit rate at 3.50 percent. The markets expect 25-50 basis points in rate hikes by the year-end.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that both the floating corridor and the relatively flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy within it, help to discourage speculative capital flows.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other BRICs, Russia has no capital controls and has pledged to keep it that way, having resisted calls to reintroduce them during the crisis.\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (FACTBOX)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110804e784001e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
