\par\par \b \uc2 Ulyukayev: Russia Saw $3 Bln Cap Inflows In June - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2011\par 09:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Russia reported $3 billion in capital inflows for June, bucking a trend that has seen more than $30 billion flee the country during the first five months of the year, First Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said Thursday, the state-run Prime Tass news agency reported.\par \par \uc2 The inflows mainly came from companies paying out dividends for the month, Ulyukayev said, adding that the number was only a preliminary estimate.\par \par \uc2 "June is always a positive month in regards to capital flows because that's when many companies pay dividends," he said. "However, we would like to underline that capital movements are becoming more balanced."\par \par \uc2 Russia saw $21.3 billion dollars in capital flows in the first quarter and $9.9 billion in the second quarter of the year, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev said he expects Russia to see a net capital outflow of $30 billion or slightly more by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought around $4 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem ruble strength in June, Ulyukayev said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the government's 400 billion ruble ($14.2 billion) bailout of troubled Bank of Moscow will not have a significant effect on inflation.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires, +7 495 232 9192;\par \par \uc2 ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com [ 07-07-11 0811GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110707e777000hx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
