\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  to top up oil fund with cbank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2011\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank to channel purchased hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into oil fund\par \par \uc2 * Oil fund unchanged for 13 months, $26.6 bln as of June 1\par \par \uc2 * Was used to prop up budget during 2008-9 crisis\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, detail)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 6 (Reuters) - Russia will replenish its oil reserve wealth fund, used to prop up the budget during the 2008-2009 crisis, with hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes to cap gains in the rouble, the bank said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 At present the proceeds of such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are transferred to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves,"\par \par \uc2 As of June 1, the fund stood at 745.86 billion roubles, or $26.57 billion. [ID:nLDE7500W6]#\par \par \uc2 Accumulated during nearly a decade of oil-fuelled economic expansion, the fund was used to prop up the budget in 2009 when the country suffered its biggest economic contraction in 15 years. The finance ministry used cash from the fund for the last time in April 2010.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the rouble in the range of 32.45-37.45 against a euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX>, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rouble trades in the lower part of the corridor and selling dollars and euros when it weakens towards the upper part.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $11.9 billion and 1.8 billion euro to limit oil-driven gains in the rouble, which has firmed around 10 percent versus the dollar <RUB=>.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya; Writing by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Lidia Kelly, John Stonestreet)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110606e766000j2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
