\par\par \b \uc2 RUSSIAN FEDERATION 7.85% BONDS DUE 10/03/2018 (144A) - Publication of Prospectus\b0\par\par\uc2 THE \b \highlight22\uc2 MINISTRY OF FINANCE\b0 \highlight\uc2  OF THE RUSSIAN FEDERATION; PR Newswire   \par \uc2 179,534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2011\par 10:07\par \uc2 PR Newswire UK Disclose\par \uc2 PRNDIS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011 PR Newswire Europe Limited.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                                                       \par \par                               Russian Federation                               \par \par                                RUB50,000,000,000                               \par \par                          7.85 per cent. Bonds due 2018                         \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (to be consolidated and form a single series on and as of the Closing Date with\f28 \par \par \uc2 the RUB40,000,000,000 7.85% Bonds due 2018 issued on 10 March 2011)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par                 Issue Price of the New Bonds: 104.515 per cent.                \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (plus interest accrued from, and including, 10 March 2011, to, but excluding, 26 May 2011)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par                               -------------------                              \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Russian Federation\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ") acting on behalf of the Russian Federation (the "Issuer," "Russia" or the "Russian Federation") is issuing an aggregate principal amount of RUB50,000,000,000 7.85 per cent. Bonds due 2018 (the "New Bonds") to be consolidated and form a single series on and as of the Closing Date (as defined below) with the RUB40,000,000,000 7.85 per cent. Bonds due 2018 issued on 10 March 2011 (the "Existing Bonds," and together with the New Bonds, the "Bonds"). Interest on the Bonds is payable semi annually in arrear on 10 March and 10 September in each year. See "Terms and Conditions of the New Bonds-Interest." Payments under the Bonds will be made, free and clear of, and without withholding or deduction for, any taxes imposed by the Russian Federation, to the extent described under "Terms and Conditions of the New Bonds-Taxation." Unless previously redeemed, or purchased and cancelled, the Bonds will be redeemed at their principal amount together with accrued interest on 10 March 2018 and are not redeemable prior to that date. See "Terms and Conditions of the New Bonds-Redemption, Purchase and Cancellation."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Applications have been made to the Financial Services Authority in its capacity as competent authority under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (the "UKLA") for the New Bonds to be admitted to the official list of the UKLA (the "Official List") and to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the "\f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  ") for the New Bonds to be admitted to trading on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Regulated Market (the "Market"). References in this Prospectus to the New Bonds being "listed" (and all related references) shall mean that the New Bonds have been admitted to the Official List and have been admitted to trading on the Market. The Market is a regulated market for the purposes of Directive 2004/39/EC (the "Markets in Financial Instruments Directive").\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEE "RISK FACTORS" FOR A DISCUSSION OF CERTAIN FACTORS TO BE CONSIDERED IN CONNECTION WITH AN INVESTMENT IN THE BONDS STARTING ON PAGE 5.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bonds have not been and will not be registered under the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  Act of 1933, as amended (the "Securities Act"), or with any securities regulatory authority of any State or other jurisdiction of the United States, and may not be offered or sold within the United States except pursuant to an exemption from, or in a transaction not subject to, the registration requirements of the Securities Act. For a summary of certain restrictions on resale, see "Subscription and Sale," "Form and Transfer of the Bonds" and "Transfer Restrictions."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Existing Bonds have been and the New Bonds will be offered and sold outside the United States in reliance on Regulation S under the Securities Act ("Regulation S") and within the United States to "qualified institutional buyers" ("QIBs") (as defined in Rule 144A under the Securities Act ("Rule 144A")) in reliance on Rule 144A. Prospective purchasers are hereby notified that sellers of the New Bonds may be relying on the exemption from the provisions of Section 5 of the Securities Act provided by Rule 144A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Existing Bonds have been and the New Bonds will be offered and sold in registered form in the denomination of RUB5,000,000. The Existing Bonds offered and sold in reliance on Regulation S (the "Existing Unrestricted Bonds") are each represented by beneficial interests in an unrestricted global bond (the "Existing Unrestricted Global Bond"). Upon issue, the New Bonds offered and sold in reliance on Regulation S (the "New Unrestricted Bonds") will each be represented by beneficial interests in a new unrestricted global bond (the "New Unrestricted Global Bond," and together with the Existing Unrestricted Global Bond, the "Unrestricted Global Bond"), in registered form without interest coupons attached, which will be registered in the name of a nominee for, and shall be deposited on or about 26 May 2011 (the "Closing Date") with a common depositary for, and in respect of interests held through, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Euroclear Bank SA/NV\f28 \uc2 \f2  ("Euroclear") and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clearstream\f28 \uc2 \f2  Banking, soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 anonyme ("\f28 \uc2 \f2 Clearstream\f28 \uc2 \f