finance the federal deficit with a combination primarily of domestic and external borrowing and privatisation sales, and, in 2011, proceeds from the Reserve Fund. The Government also expects in 2011\u8211\'20\'132013 to make drawdowns on the National Wealth Fund for the purpose of co\u8211\'20\'13financing pensions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Budget Revenue\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par The following table sets forth information regarding federal budget revenue for\par the periods indicated:\par \par                            Federal Budget Revenue(1)                           \par \par                                                 For the year                   \par                                               ended 31 December                \par                                                                                \par                                 2006      2007      2008      2009      2010   \par                                                                                \par                                             (millions of roubles)              \par                                                                                \par Total revenue                 6,278,888 7,781,120 9,275,931 7,337,751 8,305,401\par                                                                                \par Total revenue net of UST(2)   5,963,048 7,376,139 8,769,163 6,827,976 8,272,504\par                                                                                \par Tax revenue                   3,595,656 4,633,704 5,232,654 3,896,499 4,401,934\par                                                                                \par Profit taxes                    509,913   641,322   761,129   195,420   255,026\par                                                                                \par VAT                           1,510,904 2,261,477 2,132,203 2,049,964 2,498,264\par                                                       