\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Hits 2.5-Year High Against Dollar On High Oil Prices\b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 11:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble hit its strongest levels against the dollar since late 2008 Friday, bolstered by oil prices rising on turmoil in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The ruble traded at 28.05 against the dollar, strengthening 0.5% to its highest since Dec. 19, 2008. It lost ground to the euro, however, after the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on the heels of a rate rise by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "With oil at its current levels, there are not too many people willing to bet against the ruble," said Roman Pakhomenko, a dealer at \uc2 Lanta Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Political unrest in the Middle East and military action in Libya has driven the price for oil--Russia's chief export--to around $124 a barrel for Brent crude, its highest level in two-and-a-half years.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not very active on the market right now," said a dealer at a Russian bank. "Whether they will step up their level of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains to be seen."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seeking to minimize its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as it moves towards a policy of inflation targeting. The regulator purchased $10.7 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the first quarter, compared with around $60 billion in the second quarter of 2008--the last time oil prices exceeded $100 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 The ruble traded at RUB40.37 against the euro, weaker by 0.3%. It was stronger by 0.2% against a basket of euros and dollars at RUB33.60.\par \par \uc2 Russia's popularity as a safe haven amid Middle East turmoil was highlighted Friday by weekly fund flow statistics from Emerging Portfolio Investment Research. Russia-focused funds dominated their emerging market peers, drawing $400 million of inflows for the week.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232 9195; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-04-11 0909GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020110408e7480000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
