\par\par \b \uc2 Russia buys $5.4 bln to curb rouble rise in March\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2011\par 16:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Buys $4.5 bln and 0.6 bln euros to stem rouble's rise\par \par \uc2  * Rouble up 1.34 pct vs dollar, 0.1 pct vs basket in March\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, April 7 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it bought $4.49 billion and 0.6 billion euros ($0.85 billion) in March to ease upside pressure on the rouble, boosted to its strongest levels since late 2008 by rallying oil prices.\par \par \uc2  The data published on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website came in line with the figure mentioned by the bank's governor Sergei Ignatyev earlier this week. [ID:nLDE7341LH]\par \par \uc2  The data showed so-called 'target' purchases -- subject to pre-set daily limits based on factors such as the oil price and budget balance forecasts -- totalled $3.4 billion and 0.4 billion euros. \par \par \uc2  The remaining $1.2 billion and 0.2 billion euro were thus registered as 'accumulated' \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the rouble within a floating corridor versus the euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX> and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars and euros in the lower part of the band, sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the upper part and does nothing in the middle.\par \par \uc2  The corridor is moved by 5 kopecks once the amount of so-called 'accumulated' \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  tops $600 million, reflecting market trends and matching the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intention to move towards a free float.\par \par \uc2  That suggests that the floating corridor may have been moved twice to 32.35-37.35 rouble versus the basket by the end of the month from 32.45-37.45, as of March 1. [ID:nL9E7EG08K].\par \par \uc2  On the back of oil prices above $110 per barrel [O/R], the rouble had strengthened 1.34 percent versus the dollar and added 0.1 percent versus the basket.\par \par \uc2   (Writing by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Ron Askew) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110407e7470011g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
