\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Russia's rouble policy\b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 28 (Reuters) - Following are details of Russia's current \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy board member Sergei Shvetsov clarified some details of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  parameters to Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 For an INTERVIEW with Shvetsov please see [ID:nL9E7EG08K]\par \par \uc2 BASKET <RUS=MCX>\par \par \uc2 Russia introduced a basket for tracking the rouble's course on Feb. 1, 2005, initially made up of 0.1 euros and 0.9 dollars.\par \par \uc2 The euro's share was gradually increased to reach the current 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars composition on Feb. 8, 2007.\par \par \uc2 FLOATING CORRIDOR\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a floating rouble corridor in early 2010, shifting its boundaries up or down by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at, respectively, the upper or lower boundary\par \par \uc2 Between mid-February and mid-May 2010 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made 32 such steps, bringing the corridor to 33.40-36.40 roubles against the basket.\par \par \uc2 On Oct. 13, 2010, Russia widened the corridor symmetrically to 4 roubles from 3, and decreased the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  necessary for the band shift to $650 million.\par \par \uc2 From March 1, 2011, the band was widened further to 5 roubles, while the size of cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  which prompt a shift in its boundaries was reduced to $600 million. The next band widening is not planned for at least another few months.\par \par \uc2 Cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are now based on any foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales or purchases in excess of the so-called daily 'target' volumes set at each month-end based on estimates of the budget balance, Finance Ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and oil price. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not disclose these daily limits.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the corridor stands at 32.45-37.45 roubles against the basket, "plus-minus 5 kopecks," Shvetsov says.\par \par \uc2 The floating corridor itself is split into three.\par \par \uc2 When the rouble is at the weak end of the corridor, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells small volumes of dollars each day. In the one-rouble wide corridor in the middle of the band it does nothing. When the rouble is strong it buys dollars and euros.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  increase as the rouble approaches the corridor's boundaries, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing the size of its bid on the market, meaning the amount needed to shift the band is accumulated more quickly. The daily limit on planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, remains unchanged.\par \par \uc2 A wider, fixed-trading band of 26 to 41 roubles was introduced in January 2009 and scrapped in October 2010.\par \par \uc2 MOVE TOWARDS 'DIRTY' FREE FLOAT\par \par \uc2 Russia is gradually moving towards targeting inflation rather than exchange rates and the widening of the corridor is seen as the latest step in that direction.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it is aiming for a managed -- or 'dirty' -- free float and will continue to reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it deems it necessary.\par \par \uc2 Some $500 billion in gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third largest, give \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The regulator says it does not target a particular exchange rate, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are merely aimed at smoothing out excessive market volatility.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that the floating corridor and the relatively flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy within it, helps to discourage speculative capital flows.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other BRICs, Russia has no capital controls and has pledged to keep it that way, having resisted calls to reintroduce them during the crisis.\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Andrey Ostroukh and Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (FACTBOX)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110328e73s000p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
